    schema:name "HIMAWARI-3 (GMS-3)"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: Meteorology."@en,
        """GCMD definitions: The Geostationary Meteorological Satellites (GMS) were Japan&#039;s contribution to the international Global Atmospheric Research Program (GARP).  The GMS series carried the Visible and Spin Scan Radiometer (VISSR).  The satellite was spin-stabilized with a despun earth-pointing antenna.  The satellite was positioned near 140 deg E and was designed to operate for 5 years.  This was a follow-on GMS type spacecraft launched and controlled by NASDA of Japan. The spacecraft was launched in August 1984, and turned off in December 1989.
__________
