        "LAPAN-Tubsat"@en,
        "TUBSAT-7"@en ;
    schema:name "LAPAN-TUBSAT"@en ;
    mac:description """GCMD definitions: LAPAN-TUBSAT is a cooperation between TU Berlin and the National Institute of Aeronautics and Space of Indonesia (Lembaga Penerbangan dan Antariksa Nasional/LAPAN). It was launched with an Indian PSLV on Jan. 10, 2007.

It's design follows the TUBSAT family with dimensions of 45x45x27cm and a mass of about 56kg.

Mission goals:

-Technology Demonstrators
-Earth Observation
-Attitude Control Experiments 

Summary provided by: http://www.ilr.tu-berlin.de/RFA/sat/lapan/content.htm


