eor:satellite.2009-055A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "WORLDVIEW-2 (WV-2)"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "DigitalGlobe WORLDVIEW-2"@en,
        "WORLDVIEW-2"@en,
        "WorldView-2"@en,
        "Worldview 2"@en ;
    schema:name "WORLDVIEW-2 (WV-2)"@en ;
    mac:description """GCMD definitions: WorldView-2, launched October 2009, is the first high-resolution 8-band multispectral commercial satellite. Operating at an altitude of 770 kilometers, WorldView-2 provides 46 cm panchromatic resolution and 1.85 meter* multispectral resolution. WorldView-2 has an average revisit time of 1.1 days and is capable of collecting up to 1 million square kilometers of 8-band imagery per day, greatly enhancing the DigitalGlobe multispectral collection capacity for more rapid and reliable collection.

The WorldView-2 system, offering incredible accuracy, agility, capacity and spectral diversity, allows DigitalGlobe to substantially expand its imagery product offerings to both commercial and government customers.


