eor:satellite.2016-002A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "JASON-3"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "Jason 3"@en,
        "Jason-3"@en,
        "Joint Altimetry Satellite Oceanography Network - 3"@en ;
    schema:name "JASON-3"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: 3-year nominal mission lifetime, 5-year extended lifetime. Physical oceanography, geodesy/gravity, climate monitoring, marine meteorology."@en,
        "GCMD definitions: Jason-3 is the fourth mission in U.S.-European series of satellite missions that measure the height of the ocean surface. Launched on January 17, 2016, the mission will extend the time series of ocean surface topography measurements (the hills and valleys of the ocean surface) begun by the TOPEX/Poseidon satellite mission in 1992 and continuing through the Jason-1 (launched in 2001) and the currently operating OSTM/Jason-2 (launched in 2008) missions. These measurements provide scientists with critical information about circulation patterns in the ocean and about both global and regional changes in sea level and the climate implications of a warming world."@en,
        "OSCAR description: 3rd flight unit of the JASON series, also called &ldquo;Ocean Surface Topography Mission (OSTM)&rdquo;. Main mission: ocean topography and waves. Substantial contribution to Solid Earth (geoid). Significant contribution to space weather."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Spacecraft engaged in practical applications and uses of space technology such as weather or communications"@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Earth Science"@en ;
    smi:inclination "66.04"^^xsd:float ;
    smi:period "112.42"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:COSPARId "2016-002A" ;
    eo-ont:NORADId 41240 ;
    eo-ont:apogee "1344.0"^^xsd:float ;
