eor:satellite.2016-067A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "WORLDVIEW-4"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "DigitalGlobe WORLDVIEW-4"@en,
        "WorldView-4"@en ;
    schema:name "WORLDVIEW-4"@en ;
    mac:description "GCMD definitions: WorldView-4 was an imaging and environment-monitoring satellite from Maxar of the United States, which launched on 11 November 2016 to enhance European Space Imaging's customer offering with very high-resolution imagery options. Operating in coordination with WorldView-3 and the other satellites of the WorldView constellation, it offered high-resolution imagery at 31 cm resolution in panchromatic mode and 1.23 m in multispectral mode; it provided large area single pass (synoptic) collection, which eliminates temporal variations and offers geolocation accuracy and bi-directional scanning with daily revisits. On 7 January 2019, WorldView-4 was retired when the satellite experienced a failure in its CMGs (Control Moment Gyros), preventing the satellite from collecting imagery due to the loss of an axis of stability."@en,
        "OSCAR description: 4th flight unit of the WorldView programme. Renamed from GeoEye-2 in 2014. Main mission: high-resolution land observation."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Spacecraft engaged in practical applications and uses of space technology such as weather or communications"@en ;
