eor:satellite.2017-064A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "SENTINEL-5P"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "Sentinel 5 Precursor"@en,
        "Sentinel 5P"@en,
        "Sentinel-5 Precursor"@en,
        "Sentinel-5 precursor"@en,
        "Sentinel-5P"@en ;
    schema:name "SENTINEL-5P"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: Sentinel-5P performs atmospheric measurements with high spatio-temporal resolution, to be used for air quality, ozone & UV radiation, and climate monitoring & forecasting in support of the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS)."@en,
        """GCMD definitions: A precursor satellite mission, Sentinel-5P aims to fill in the data gap and provide data continuity between the retirement of the Envisat satellite and NASA's Aura mission and the launch of Sentinel-5. The mission will perform atmospheric monitoring and was launched in October 2017.

Launch Date: 13 October 2017

Operational lifespan: 7 years

Mission Objectives:

The Sentinel-5 Precursor objectives are to provide operational space-borne observations in support to the operational monitoring of:

Air Quality
Ozone and Surface UV
Climate
It will provide measurements of:

Ozone
NO_2
SO_2
Formaldehyde
Aerosol
Carbonmonoxide
Methane
Clouds
Mission Orbit:

Orbit Type: Sun-synchronous, polar
Orbit Height: 824 km
Inclination: 98.74°
Repeat Cycle: 16 days Mean LST: 13:30 at Ascending Node
Sentinel-5 Precursor is foreseen to operate in loose formation with Suomi-NPP

 

Payload:

The TROPOMI instrument is a UV-VIS-NIR-SWIR push-broom grating spectrometer.

Spectral range: 270-495 nm, 710-775 nm, 2305-2385 nm
Spectral resolution: 0.25-0.55 nm
Observation mode: nadir pointing, global daily coverage, 7x7 km^2 ground
Payload Mass: 200kg
Configuration:
The spacecraft launch mass is ~900 kg

Launch vehicle: 
ROCKOT

Contractors:

Prime Contractor: Airbus Defence & Space
TROPOMI contract: Dutch Ministry of Economic Affairs"""@en,
        "OSCAR description: Single flight unit of the Sentinel-5P programme. Main mission: atmospheric chemistry."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: The Sentinel-5P satellite mission forms part of the European Copernicus programme. It is the first Copernicus mission dedicated to monitoring the atmosphere. Sentinel-5P makes use of a Tropomi spectrometer to map every day, in the global atmosphere, trace gases affecting the air such as nitrogen dioxide, ozone, formaldehyde, sulphur dioxide, methane, carbon monoxide, and aerosols. Sentinel-5P detects pollution over cities and contributes to services such as volcanic ash monitoring for aviation safety and for services that warn of high levels of ultraviolet radiation. Pursuant to the Agreement between the European Union, represented by the European Commission, and the European Space Agency on the Implementation of the Copernicus Programme, including the Transfer of Ownership of the Sentinels (Copernicus Agreement), which entered into force on 28 October 2014, ownership of Sentinel-5P was transferred to the European Union at the moment of lift-off of the satellite’s launch vehicle."@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Earth Science"@en ;
    smi:inclination "98.76"^^xsd:float ;
    smi:period "101.44"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:COSPARId "2017-064A" ;
    eo-ont:NORADId 42969 ;
    eo-ont:apogee "828.0"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:dataPortal "https://browser.dataspace.copernicus.eu/"^^xsd:anyURI,
        "https://s5phub.copernicus.eu/dhus/#/home"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    eo-ont:dryMass "738.0"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:ect "13:30:00"^^xsd:time ;
    eo-ont:launchDate "2017-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    eo-ont:launchMass "820.0"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:launchSite eor:launch_site.PLMSC ;
    eo-ont:operationalStatus eor:operational_status.operational ;
    eo-ont:orbitAltitude "824.0"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:orbitSense "Ascending"@en ;
    eo-ont:orbitType eor:orbit_type.LEO_S ;
    eo-ont:owner eor:owner.ESA ;
    eo-ont:perigee "826.0"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:relatedSatId "CEOS:581",
        "GCMD:77e9a75e-2c3b-428b-8b21-b6a902dd8fee",
        "ITC:satellite-310",
        "OSCAR:sentinel_5p" ;
    eo-ont:satelliteAgency "ESA, COM, NSO"@en ;
    eo-ont:webInfo "https://earth.esa.int/web/guest/missions/esa-eo-missions/sentinel-5p"^^xsd:anyURI,
        "https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/missions/sentinel-5p"^^xsd:anyURI .

