eor:satellite.2018-070A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "ICESAT-2"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "ICESAT 2"@en,
        "ICESat-2"@en,
        "Ice, Cloud and land Elevation Satellite"@en,
        "Ice, Cloud, and Land Elevation Satellite 2"@en,
        "Ice, Cloud, and land Elevation Satellite-2"@en,
        "Icesat-2"@en ;
    schema:name "ICESAT-2"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: 3-year nominal mission life, 5-year goal. Continue the assessment of polar ice changes and measure vegetation canopy heights, allowing estimates of biomass and carbon in aboveground vegetation in conjunction with related missions, and allow measurements of solid earth properties."@en,
        """GCMD definitions: [Text Source: NASA ICESat-2, https://icesat-2.gsfc.nasa.gov/ ]

ICESat-2 will provide scientists with height measurements that create a global portrait of Earth’s 3rd dimension, 
gathering data that can precisely track changes of terrain including glaciers, sea ice, forests and more.

While many of ICESat-2’s discoveries are yet to be imagined, the satellite mission has four science objectives:

Measure melting ice sheets and investigate how this effects sea level rise,
Measure and investigate changes in the mass of ice sheets and glaciers,
Estimate and study sea ice thickness,
Measure the height of vegetation in forests and other ecosystems worldwide.

Group: Platform_Details
   Entry_ID: ICESAT-II
   Group: Platform_Identification
      Platform_Category: Earth Observation Satellites
      Platform_Series_or_Entity: NASA Decadal Survey
      Short_Name: ICESAT-II
      Long_Name: Ice, Cloud and Land Elevation Satellite-II
   End_Group
   Creation_Date: 2009-02-25
   Online_Resource: https://icesat-2.gsfc.nasa.gov/
   Group: Platform_Logistics
      Launch_Date: 2018
      Primary_Sponsor: USA/NASA
   End_Group
End_Group"""@en,
        "OSCAR description: 2nd flight unit of the ICESat programme. Main mission; polar ice observation and ice sheet mass balance, with capability to derive sea ice thickness. Sustantial contribution to cloud and aerosol profiling Significant contribution to land topography and vegetation canopy."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Spacecraft engaged in practical applications and uses of space technology such as weather or communications"@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Science"@en,
        "UCS Users: Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Laser Imaging"@en ;
