eor:satellite.2018-076A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "SAOCOM 1A"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "SAOCOM-1A"@en,
        "SAR Observation & Communications Satellite-1A"@en,
        "SAtélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas - 1A"@en,
        "Satélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas 1A"@en,
        "Satélite Argentino de Observación Con Microondas"@en ;
    schema:name "SAOCOM 1A"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: Earth observation and emergency management with an L-band SAR, soil moisture for agriculture and hydrology (main driver), interferometry."@en,
        """GCMD definitions: The SAOCOM (SAtélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas) satellite series represents Argentina's approved polarimetric L-band SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) constellation of two spacecraft, a program defined, managed and operated by CONAE (Comisión Nacional de Actividades Espaciales), Argentina's Space Agency, Buenos Aires. The SAOCOM-1 mission is composed of two satellites (SAOCOM-1A and -1B). The overall objective of is to provide an effective Earth observation and disaster monitoring capability.

SAOCOM -1A features six computers that work in synchronicity; the spacecraft has a mass of 3,000 kg. Its antenna, designed in central Cordoba province, is composed of 140 smaller antennas. As many as 600 Argentine professionals have been working on the $500 million-satellite since 2011."""@en,
        "OSCAR description: 1st flight unit of the SAOCOM programme. Main mission: hydrology and land observation. Substantial contribution to surveillance and emergency management."@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Radar Imaging"@en ;
    smi:inclination "97.89"^^xsd:float ;
