eor:satellite.2018-099AU a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "ICEYE-X2"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "ICEYE"@en,
        "ICEYE POC 2"@en ;
    schema:name "ICEYE-X2"@en ;
    mac:description "GCMD definitions: ICEYE's overall mission is to enable better decision making for everyone by providing timely and reliable Earth observation data. To achieve that goal, the company is developing its own synthetic-aperture radar (SAR) sensor technologies suitable for satellites under 100kg in weight. ICEYE is building a constellation of 18 SAR satellite by end of 2020 and that will enable a 3 hour on average revisit rate around the globe."@en,
        "OSCAR description: Constellation of micro-satellites, proof-of-concept of a sustainable operational SAR constellation. Orbit heights generally sunsynchronous with height from 500 to 700 km, and ECT  conditioned by the launch of opportunity. Main missions: all-weather high-resolution land observation; sea-ice. Substantial contribution to disaster monitoring."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Experimental satellite, carrying a synthetic aperture radar. Data will be provided commercially."@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Commercial"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Radar Imaging (SAR)"@en ;
