eor:satellite.2020-059A a eo-ont:Satellite ;
    rdfs:label "SAOCOM 1B"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "SAOCOM-1B"@en,
        "SAR Observation & Communications Satellite-1B"@en,
        "SAtélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas - 1B"@en,
        "Satélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas 1B"@en,
        "Satélite Argentino de Observación Con Microondas"@en ;
    schema:name "SAOCOM 1B"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: Earth observation and emergency management with an L-band SAR, soil moisture for agriculture and hydrology (main driver), interferometry."@en,
        """GCMD definitions: The SAOCOM (SAtélite Argentino de Observación COn Microondas) satellite series represents Argentina's approved polarimetric L-band SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) constellation of two spacecraft, a program defined, managed and operated by CONAE (Comisión Nacional de Actividades Espaciales), Argentina's Space Agency, Buenos Aires. The SAOCOM-1 mission is composed of two satellites (SAOCOM-1A and -1B). The overall objective of is to provide an effective Earth observation and disaster monitoring capability.

SAOCOM 1-B is expected to be launched in 2019, followed by another two satellites as part of the SAOCOM 2 series, which will have the experiences collected from the first mission built in. Both INVAP and CONAE have ample experience in designing satellites and in space missions, as they developed the SAC-B, SAC-A, SAC-C and SAC-D Aquarius satellites."""@en,
        "OSCAR description: 2nd flight unit of the SAOCOM programme, companion of SAOCOM-1A. Main mission: hydrology and land observation. Substantial contribution to surveillance and emergency management."@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Earth observation. Main functions are measurement of soil moisture, emergency management, mapping of forest cover and water resource surveying"@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Radar Imaging"@en ;
    smi:inclination "97.89"^^xsd:float ;
    smi:period "97.16"^^xsd:float ;
    eo-ont:COSPARId "2020-059A" ;
