    rdfs:label "CSG-2"@en ;
    schema:alternateName "COSMO-SkyMed Second Generation - 2"@en,
        "COSMO-Skymed FM2"@en,
        "COSMO-Skymed Second Gen FM2"@en,
        "CSG FM2"@en ;
    schema:name "CSG-2"@en ;
    mac:description "CEOS applications: Environmental monitoring, surveillance and risk management applications, environmental resources management, maritime management, earth topographic mapping, law enforcement, informative / science applications."@en,
        "OSCAR description: 2nd (last) flight unit of the COSMO-SkyMed SG programme. Main mission: surveillance and emergency management."@en,
        """OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Earth observation (radar)
The COSMO-SkyMed Second Generation (CSG) is due to be a constellation of 4 satellites, aimed at
enhancing the quality and capability of imaging of the original 4-spacecraft COSMO-SkyMed
constellation (CSK). The satellites, each with a design life of 7 years, were developed by the Italian
Space Agency (ASI) with funding from the Italian Ministry of Defense and the Italian Ministry of
Research for both military and civil use. The first two satellites were launched in 2019 and 2022, with
the remaining two due to be launched in 2024 and 2025."""@en,
        "UCS Purpose: Earth Observation"@en,
        "UCS Users: Military/Government"@en,
        "UCS detailedPurpose: Radar Imaging"@en ;
    smi:inclination "97.89"^^xsd:float ;
    smi:period "97.16"^^xsd:float ;
