    mac:description "CEOS applications: NACHOS (Nano-satellite Atmospheric Chemistry Hyperspectral Observation System) is a pair of high-resolution hyperspectral imaging CubeSats developed by Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL) and NASA to help climate and volcanic research. The satellites were launched in February and July 2022, each with a design life of three to five years. NACHOS-1 completed its mission in July 2024."@en,
        "OSCAR description: First of 2 3U cubesats to develop hyperspectral imaging of atmospheric trace gases. Significant contribution to atmospheric chemistry and air quality"@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Spacecraft engaged in investigation of spaceflight techniques and technology"@en ;
