        "Argos-4 also referred to as GAzelle"@en,
        "GAzelle"@en ;
    schema:name "OTB-3-GAZELLE"@en ;
    mac:description "OSCAR description: Continuation of the NOAA/CNES ARGOS program to collect a variety of data from both stationary and mobile transmitters around the world.  Applications include <a href=\"http://www.argos-system.org/applications-argos/\">Environmental monitoring applications</a>, <a href=\"http://www.argos-system.org/applications-argos/marine-fisheries/\">Marine fisheries applications</a>, <a href=\"http://www.argos-system.org/applications-argos/maritime-security/\">Maritime security applications</a>, <a href=\"http://www.argos-system.org/applications-argos/offshore/\">Offshore applications</a> and <a href=\"http://www.argos-system.org/applications-argos/humanitarian-aid/\">Humanitarian Aid</a>. In contrast to previous DCS/ARGOS instruments on NOAA platforms this is a small satellite on which the DCS/ARGOS system is mounted.  First of a planned constellation of 25 ARGOS-4 satellites which are planned by 2024 Details here: https://www.nesdis.noaa.gov/next-generation/argos-4-launch"@en,
        "OSOidx functionOfSpaceObject: Spacecraft engaged in practical applications and uses of space technology such as weather or communications"@en ;
    smi:inclination "98.37"^^xsd:float ;
    smi:period "99.83"^^xsd:float ;
